# Copy to .env next to compose.yaml (scripts/setup-mac-mini.sh does this for you), then
#   chmod 600 .env
# .env is ignored by git. Never commit it, never paste its contents anywhere.
# In host mode, the default, nothing here is secret and every line is optional: scripts/update.sh
# writes NEBOTOK_DIGEST and creates the default backup folder.

# The image digest to run (sha256:...). Written by scripts/update.sh after it has verified the
# image was built by this repo's CI. Do not edit by hand; use scripts/update.sh or rollback.sh.
NEBOTOK_DIGEST=

# The folder on the Mac where Litestream keeps the backups: a copy of the database a few seconds
# behind, 7 days of history, and the last 30 nightly snapshots. A full path to a folder that exists,
# readable by you only. Without this line it is ~/NebotokBackups, which scripts/update.sh creates.
# Keep it inside your home folder, so Time Machine backs it up too. See docs/deploy.md, "Backups".
# BACKUP_DIR=/Users/REPLACE_ME/NebotokBackups

# Optional: the port on 127.0.0.1 where the game is published, and where scripts/serve.sh points
# this Mac's Tailscale (HTTPS port 8445). Change it only if 8567 is taken.
# NEBOTOK_PORT=8567

# Optional: the first three numbers of the stack's Docker network, 10.231.67.0/28 by default. The
# game trusts forwarded client addresses only from its gateway (.1). Change it only if Docker reports
# that the range overlaps another network, or for a second test stack on the same Mac.
# NEBOTOK_NETWORK=10.231.67

# ── Sidecar mode only ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The game as its own Tailscale device instead of behind this Mac's Tailscale (docs/deploy.md,
# "Sidecar mode"). `scripts/setup-mac-mini.sh --sidecar` writes these three.
# Docker Compose reads COMPOSE_FILE itself, so every docker compose command and script uses both files.
# COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yaml:compose.tailscale.yaml
# Tailscale auth key for the game's own tailnet device. Create it in the Tailscale admin console:
# Settings > Keys > Generate auth key, with Tags = tag:nebotok and Pre-approved on. Reusable and
# Ephemeral off. See deploy/tailscale/policy.md. It is used once, for the first login only.
# TS_AUTHKEY=tskey-auth-REPLACE_ME
# The device name on the tailnet. The game is then at https://<TS_HOSTNAME>.<your tailnet>.ts.net
# TS_HOSTNAME=nebotok

# ── Local test only (compose.local.yaml) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# npm run verify:container sets these per worktree (a free port, its own image tag and network),
# so several checks can run at once. Set them only to test the image by hand.
# The local port for testing the image on this computer.
# NEBOTOK_LOCAL_PORT=2567
# The image tag the local stack builds and runs.
# NEBOTOK_LOCAL_IMAGE=nebotok:local
# The first three numbers of the local stack's network (its .16/28), trusted gateway .17.
# NEBOTOK_LOCAL_NETWORK=10.231.67
# A separate, empty folder for the local test's backups. Never BACKUP_DIR.
# npm run verify:container sets its own temporary one.
# NEBOTOK_LOCAL_BACKUP_DIR=/tmp/nebotok-local-backups
